WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Connect an AWS account to CryoLauncher.
Why: Cloud runs use this account through temporary access to an AWS role.
Look for: Start signed in to CryoStack and to an AWS account you are authorized to connect.

2
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:22.000
Choose Cloud in the Mode panel.
Why: Cloud mode reveals the AWS account connection controls.
Look for: Scroll to Environment → AWS ACCOUNT.

3
00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Under AWS ACCOUNT, choose Connect AWS Account.
Why: CryoStack creates a setup link tied to your signed-in user.
Look for: Awaiting role means you can continue to Open AWS Setup.

4
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Choose Open AWS Setup.
Why: The button opens the connection-specific CloudFormation setup in a new tab.
Look for: Switch to the AWS tab showing Quick create stack.

5
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:59.000
Review the prefilled Quick create stack page.
Why: The generated template links your AWS access role to this CryoStack connection.
Look for: Keep the generated stack name and connection parameters; confirm the intended AWS account.

6
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:13.000
Review the IAM notice, then check its acknowledgement.
Why: CloudFormation needs your permission to create the access role.
Look for: The acknowledgement checkbox is checked.

7
00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Choose Create stack.
Why: This submits the access-role stack you just reviewed.
Look for: AWS starts creating the stack; wait for completion.

8
00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:33.000
Wait until the new stack shows CREATE_COMPLETE.
Why: The role must exist before CryoStack can verify its access.
Look for: CREATE_COMPLETE is visible for the created stack.

9
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:43.000
Open the Outputs tab on that stack.
Why: Outputs contains the role identifier to return to CryoStack.
Look for: Find the row whose Key is RoleArn.

10
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:59.000
Select the Value in the RoleArn row; press Ctrl+C or Command+C.
Why: CryoStack needs the full ARN of the access role created by this stack.
Look for: Copy the entire value, not the RoleArn key; its private contents are hidden here.

11
00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:16.000
Return to CryoStack and paste the full value into Role ARN.
Why: This selects the role CryoStack will use for temporary AWS access.
Look for: The Role ARN field is filled; its contents are hidden in this guide.

12
00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:26.000
Choose Verify connection and wait for the check.
Why: CryoStack tests access through the newly created role.
Look for: Verifying changes to Connected when verification succeeds.

13
00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:39.000
Confirm Connected and check Last verified.
Why: This confirms access through the role you just created.
Look for: Connected, Temporary role and an updated Last verified time.

14
00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:49.000
Continue with cloud preparation and your model tutorial.
Why: A verified account is the starting point for readiness checks and paid cloud runs.
Look for: Check the connected account, resources and launch estimate before submitting a job.
